# Web Forge launch rules

Read **`RULEBOOK.md`** at the repo root before shipping **any site or page** (current or future).

**Agent docs: English.** **Site copy for .cz clients: Czech.**

## Turnstile (mandatory on every form)

- Server: `verifyTurnstile()` in `packages/form-engine/src/handler.ts`
- Client: `public/form.js` + `<div data-turnstile />` on every `[data-form]`
- Layout: `data-turnstile-site-key={process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY ?? ""}`
- CSP allows `https://challenges.cloudflare.com`
- Production: both Turnstile env vars set; never ship test keys to prod

## Pre-launch audit (mandatory before deploy)

1. **view-source** — all paths in `<site>/audit-pages.txt`
2. **Multi-perspective review** — security, performance, SEO/a11y per saved HTML
3. **External tools** — PageSpeed, securityheaders.com, Mozilla Observatory, SSL Labs on live URL

```bash
./scripts/launch-audit.sh https://www.<domain>.cz --file <site>/audit-pages.txt
```

When adding a **new page**, add its path to `audit-pages.txt` and re-run the audit.

## New site

Follow `docs/NEW-SITE.md` and `RULEBOOK.md` §5.

## Do not launch if

- Turnstile test key in production HTML
- Form without Turnstile mount
- Security Headers grade F
- TLS/DNS still on old hosting
